expr main <([your, yr, ur] welcome [back, here, anytime, (any time), (to VERB)]), ([your, yr, ur])>

let message "Use the contraction `you're` (you are) here."
let description "Catches `your welcome to` and similar, where the sentence means `you are welcome`."
let kind "Grammar"
let becomes "you're"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "Your welcome to join us anytime." "You're welcome to join us anytime."
test "your welcome to come along." "you're welcome to come along."
test "Your welcome back." "You're welcome back."
test "Your welcome here." "You're welcome here."
test "Your welcome anytime." "You're welcome anytime."
test "Your welcome any time." "You're welcome any time."
test "ur welcome to stay." "you're welcome to stay."
test "Feel free, your welcome to ask questions." "Feel free, you're welcome to ask questions."
test "Your welcome to bring a friend." "You're welcome to bring a friend."
test "Your welcome to leave early." "You're welcome to leave early."
test "Please know your welcome to visit." "Please know you're welcome to visit."

allows "You're welcome to join us anytime."
allows "Your welcome message was warm."
allows "Your welcome speech was short."
allows "Thank you for your welcome."
allows "I appreciated your welcome to the team."
allows "Your welcome email arrived."
